&lt;p&gt;We are looking for a &lt;strong&gt;Development Associate &lt;/strong&gt;to join our growing superstar Oncology Development and Process Engineering team in support of clinical patient testing in our high throughput CLIA lab.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role will enable an individual to gain both deep and broad experience in the areas of molecular assay development, data analysis, experimental design, and automation. The work we do is rewarding and fast paced. It presents many opportunities to deepen your knowledge of the field. This is an on-site role and will require the majority of days to be spent in the Menlo Park office.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Assay &amp;amp; Method Development: &lt;/strong&gt;Develop and extend current assays to better fit evolving clinical needs, with support from scientists, engineers, and other technical staff&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Computational Data Analysis: &lt;/strong&gt;Apply the analytical and computational methods used in current assays, and build upon them to enable new capabilities; develop, implement, and use software tools to quantitatively analyze experiments and processes, requiring moderate proficiency in R or Python&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Validation &amp;amp; Regulatory Compliance: &lt;/strong&gt;Support assay validations and derisking under regulatory and design control frameworks (FDA, MolDx, &lt;em&gt;etc&lt;/em&gt;.)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Scientific Communication: &lt;/strong&gt;Present technical findings and project updates verbally at group meetings and via internal written reports&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Wet Lab Execution: &lt;/strong&gt;Carry out experiments in lab and document experimental procedures and results, and contribute to routine organization of the R&amp;amp;D lab&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Tech Transfer:&lt;/strong&gt; Partner across departments to transfer and scale developed assays and workflows into high-throughput clinical laboratory operations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Troubleshooting &amp;amp; Root Cause Analysis&lt;/strong&gt;: Apply sound engineering practices to scale, optimize, and improve molecular biology methods; systematically identify and investigate root sources of variation to develop short-term corrections and long-term preventative measures&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Requirements:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor’s, Master’s, or equivalent degree in Molecular Biology, Biochemistry, Cell Biology, Microbiology, Biophysics, or related fields&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;At least 12 months of experience with molecular biology techniques (&lt;em&gt;e.g&lt;/em&gt;. PCR, electrophoresis, DNA purifications) in a research or clinical laboratory (can be during or after Bachelor’s degree)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Solid foundation in quantitative data analysis, statistics, and experimental design, with familiarity using R or Python (and a strong willingness to expand computational skills).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Clear verbal and written communication skills in reporting to cross-functional teams of scientists and non-scientists&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven experimental troubleshooting and root-cause analysis skills with sharp attention to detail&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Nice-To-Haves:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Start-up experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with next-generation sequencing (NGS) and/or cell-free DNA&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Previous experience with liquid handling or other laboratory automation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Knowledge of molecular oncology&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with composing protocols of standard molecular biology techniques&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
