&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with bioinformatics, R&amp;amp;D, and medical affairs on assay development and interpretation guidelines; serve as a subject-matter expert on oncology variant interpretation (AMP/CAP/NYS guidelines).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Qualifications:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Doctoral degree (PhD, MD, or equivalent) in genetics, molecular biology, or a related field, with board certification (ABMGG, ABP in Molecular Genetic Pathology, or equivalent).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Valid or eligible for California Clinical Laboratory Director license (CGMB, CGMBS, MD/DO licensure) and New York State CoQ in oncology testing.&lt;/li&gt;
